The concurrency tests fork a process per racer. How many a machine tolerates
is a property of the machine, not of pidly: a proot sandbox falls over well
before a workstation does, and capping the suite at the sandbox's limit makes
the locking tests weaker everywhere else.

PIDLY_TEST_RACE sets it. An exported value wins, then .env at the repo root,
then the default of 32 in tests/config.sh. .env is gitignored because it
describes one machine; .env.example is committed because the knob is not
obvious.

config.sh finds the repo root by walking up for bin/pidly rather than from
$0. It is sourced, so $0 belongs to the caller — run.sh cds into tests/
before sourcing, and resolving from $0 silently gave it a different answer
than the suites it was about to run.

Done: tests/config.sh, .env.example, wired into claim.sh and new.sh.
